<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lashio</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lashio is the largest town of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shan-state">Shan State</a> in Myanmar. It was the starting point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> Road, built in 1937–1938 to carry supplies from the railhead at Lashio to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kunming">Kunming</a> in Nationalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>; Japanese forces captured it in April 1942, cutting the route. It has a large Chinese community and is a centre of trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lashio.jpg" alt="Lashio" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: nico · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lashio_sight_IMG_0595.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
